Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:42:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(ngap): PDU Session Resource Modify Response with
 failed PDU sessions

Decode the optional PDUSessionResourceFailedToModifyListModRes (TS 38.413
9.2.1.6) and give each failed PDU session with its PDU Session Resource Modify
Unsuccessful Transfer (9.3.4.8). User Location Information and Criticality
Diagnostics are accepted (not used).

The receiver takes the criticality of each IE from the specification (all
"ignore" in this message) and no longer requires a particular value from the
sender: a RAN UE NGAP ID sent with "ignore", as TS 38.413 specifies, made the
whole message undecodable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013UXVKWJNq3UC36dmrQjjV3
